  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nIn the formal `F2[GL_2(F2)]` rank-one-idempotent register model with free scalar\n`GL_r(F2)` mixing (paid calls `I + ([g]+1)N`, `g in {a,b}`, `N = v phi` any binary\nrank-one idempotent), the **even** order-3 diagonal targets\n`T_t = diag([c],...,[c])`, `c = ab = (ba)^2`, at exactly `r = t` registers (all\nregisters arbitrary dirty inputs restored exactly) need exactly **`2t` paid\ncalls** for `t = 1, 2, 3, 4` (minima 2, 4, 6, 8). This is the first even-target\ntuple class of the coordinate-CNOT line: since `c` is even, the sign quotient\nmaps the target to `I`, so the inherited invariants flip (`q` even,\n`sum_i N_i = 0`) and no predecessor conclusion transfers. Cross-register\nsharing does not beat the two-calls-per-target tariff through `t = 4`.\n\nWritten invariants (package README sections 2-3): L1' sign-quotient parity\n(`q = 0 mod 2`); L2' free mixing forced to `U = I` with `sum_i N_i = 0`; and a\ncomplete degree 1-3 free-layer system in `F_2<x,y>/(x^2,y^2)` with the two\nkernel corrections `R = xyx + yxy + x + y` and `Z = z + z^2 + z^3`,\n`z = x + y + xy`, checked on every attaining word and rejected on a\nwrong-target control.\n\nExclusion evidence (`research/even-target-cnot-census/`, standard library only):\ncomplete natural-image meets (a homomorphic image, so empty meets exclude the\nformal word) give zero hits at `q = 2` for `t = 1, 2, 3, 4`, `q = 4` for\n`t = 3, 4`, and `q = 6` for `t = 4`; the completeness argument for cross-depth\nvalue recurrence (`C C = I`, `C C C = C`) is in README section 4. Every\nattaining word is verified exactly in `M_r(F2[G])` by an independently written\nformal-coefficient engine, with drop-one-call mutations failing. Engine B\nagrees with engine A on every small meet (including the seven 2+2 pairs at\n`t = 2`). Calibration: the exact-depth ball *value* counts at `r = 4`\n(240 / 32,651 / 3,639,920) match the recorded counts in\nhttps://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1705 exactly.\n\nValidation on the committed head:\n\n- `python3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/even-target-cnot-census`\n  passes (`PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/even-target-cnot-census\n  outcome=completed`), and `--check-only` passes metadata and pins.\n- `python3 -I -B research/even-target-cnot-census/verify.py --check-receipt`\n  prints `PASS_EVEN_TARGET_CNOT_CENSUS t1r1_min=2 t2r2_min=4 t3r3_min=6\n  t4r4_upper=8 t4r4_excluded={2: 0, 4: 0, 6: 0} balls4=240,32651,3639920\n  pr1705_ball_match=True no_new_kappa` (about 50 s).\n- `python3 -I -B research/even-target-cnot-census/test_verify.py` passes 7\n  tests including drop-one, wrong-label, wrong-target, an `|`/`^` confusion\n  regression control, and receipt-mutation rejection.\n\nReproduce:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/even-target-cnot-census\n```\n\n## Task card, overlap and limits\n\nTask `bit-new-register-model` (chooser track `bit-mechanisms`, OS nonce\n`96dd0470d4d1febfb9db9174583232e0`, priority revision 3), refined inside its\nallowed \"fixed larger register count / specified nonabelian operation family\"\nvariation to the even order-3 target class; the local task card is\n`research/even-target-cnot-census/TASK.md`. Concurrent work on other objects of\nthe same line is credited and untouched: the balanced ten-call four-SWAP\nresidual (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1317#discussioncomment-18919080),\nthe label-saturation proof (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1722),\nthe `UT_3(F2)` commutator line (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1478,\nhttps://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1573), and 1337isnot1337's\nheterogeneous `GL_2`/`AGL_2` tuple claims in\nhttps://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1317. A final\n`find_overlap.py --refresh` (complete pagination, 435 open PRs / 396 discussion\nrecords at 2026-10-14T09:10Z) found no competing even-target claim.\n\nLimits: `t = 5` and `r > t` are untouched; nothing is claimed for other target\ntuples or alphabets; no physical/compiler/hosting/precision admission, no\nsupplier or paid-moment change, no kappa and no selected-frontier change. The\n`q*(t) = 2t` statement for `t >= 5` is open.\n\nCredit Gareth Davidson (@bitplane, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1333)\nfor the model question and scalar normalization; commdata2338\n(https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1414,\nhttps://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1491,\nhttps://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1495,\nhttps://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1496), Cinna Davis\n(https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1541), Aaron Wang\n(https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1705, ball-count\ncalibration), Ross Richardson (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1722),\njuper997 (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1478) and\nsteph4n-gh (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1573) for the\nsurrounding register-model line; Ali Romman, eumemic and David Govea for the\nretained lineage. No predecessor executable is imported.\n\nContributed by **Aaron Wang** with help from opencode. Apache-2.0.\n",
